# Rank 1602 / CVE-2023-30839: PrestaShop's database helper enforced
# its SELECT-only contract only in development mode, so in production
# any caller sliding a write statement through the read API had it
# executed verbatim (SQL injection escalation through a dev-only
# guard, CWE-89/CWE-964; GHSA-p379-cxqh-q822). executeS in
# classes/db/Db.php detected non-select statements with
# preg_match('#^\s*\(?\s*(select|show|explain|describe|desc|checksum)
# \s#i', $sql) and did `if (defined('_PS_MODE_DEV_') && _PS_MODE_DEV_)
# { throw new PrestaShopDatabaseException('Db->executeS() must be
# used only with select, show, explain or describe queries'); }
# return $this->execute($sql, $use_cache);` -- the production path
# runs the statement. Pool commit d1d27dc371 is the real fix
# (COMMIT_OK -- the GHSA merge, "Fix executeS method making sure it
# does selection only"): the conditional and the fallthrough are
# deleted; the method always throws on a non-selection statement. No
# pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, mode-conditional enforcement, held on recheck. The guard
# exists and detects the violation -- its throw is wrapped in a
# development-mode conditional, the same release-mode-guard family as
# rank 1543 (orjson's debug_assert): no rule can ask "is this check
# compiled out or bypassed in production configurations" --
# mode-conditionality of guards is environment vocabulary. Measured
# at the span tip on the real checkout (3 x --cache off per revision,
# timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB): classes/db/Db.php alone and the whole
# classes/db directory both report zero findings at both revisions;
# the earlier pass's five php-heuristic findings no longer reproduce.
# The label view is identical across the revisions: code.SqlExecution
# on the five $this->query(...) calls (Db.php:545/567/614/664/744
# vulnerable, :610 shifted in the fixed file), RegexCompileSink plus
# core.PathAccessCheck on the preg_match guard, FileInclude at :281
# -- and the deleted fallthrough $this->execute($sql, $use_cache)
# carries no label at all: the PHP SQL sink family binds
# query/exec/prepare, not execute. A caller-side route was measured
# with a $_GET-fed statement through Db::getInstance()->executeS(...):
# zero findings at both revisions and trace reports the source
# reaches no sink, and resolution would not help -- the fixed revision
# still passes the string to the labelled $this->query($sql), because
# executing a tainted SELECT is the read API's contract; the taint
# axis cannot separate a write statement from a select statement. No
# guard-mode vocabulary exists in any language (code.DebugEnabled is
# a python debug-flag-exposure binding, the opposite direction), and
# a shape rule "a throw under a development-mode conditional" was
# measured on this very repository: eight sites wrap a throw in
# _PS_MODE_DEV_ at the vulnerable revision -- classes/Hook.php:548,
# classes/Tools.php:1126, config/smartyadmin.config.inc.php:112/128,
# config/smartyfront.config.inc.php:198/214 and Db.php:607 -- of
# which every one but Db.php is intentional dev-only error verbosity,
# so the rule fires eight times for one security enforcement and the
# discriminator (what the throw protects) has no fact. A binding on
# PrestaShop's own executeS would detect this platform rather than
# the weakness. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry: no taint path is
# interrupted -- the missing piece is environment vocabulary, not a
# localized construct. No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1602
# records the dev-only throw with its execute fallthrough and the
# unconditional form, both asserting reject VYQL-INJ-001: when
# guard-mode vocabulary lands, the conditional form must flip to
# expect.

test "rank1602: the select-only check throws in dev mode alone"
  lang php
  file classes/db/Db.php
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  <?php

  class Db
  {
      public function executeS($sql, $array = true, $use_cache = true)
      {
          // This method must be used only with queries which display results
          if (!preg_match('#^\s*\(?\s*(select|show|explain|describe|desc|checksum)\s#i', $sql)) {
              if (defined('_PS_MODE_DEV_') && _PS_MODE_DEV_) {
                  throw new PrestaShopDatabaseException('Db->executeS() must be used only with select, show, explain or describe queries');
              }

              return $this->execute($sql, $use_cache);
          }

          $this->result = $this->query($sql);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1602: the fixed revision always refuses non-selection statements"
  lang php
  file classes/db/Db.php
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  <?php

  class Db
  {
      public function executeS($sql, $array = true, $use_cache = true)
      {
          // This method must be used only with queries which display results
          if (!preg_match('#^\s*\(?\s*(select|show|explain|describe|desc|checksum)\s#i', $sql)) {
              throw new PrestaShopDatabaseException('Db->executeS() must be used only with select, show, explain or describe queries');
          }

          $this->result = $this->query($sql);
      }
  }
  ```
